From de3fc139c91fd40374bd1a021100866275765ae0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:38:52 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Texture packs: packs keyed with hash = quick are matched by
 picture

- PPSSPP's first hash, quick, is not computed here, so such packs were
  refused. Their keys' first halves (dimension and palette) are the same
  with any hash; only the data halves differ. A quick pack now loads:
  its keys with no data half are used as they are, and each texture
  those do not cover is compared with the pack's images by picture the
  first time it is drawn (host/gpu/texture_pack_match.cpp).
- Index: every image is shrunk to a 16x16 signature and a thumbnail of
  at most 64 pixels, on up to three threads, and saved as
  textures/.matched/<pack id>.index (the id is the xxh64 of
  textures.ini), so only new or changed images are read again.
- Match: on the matcher's thread, the four closest signatures among the
  images of the texture's shape whose keys can name it (same first
  half, zero, or zero address half), then their thumbnails. Accepted
  when the score is below 45, the next is 1.7 times further off or the
  same picture, and at most 8% of the blurred picture differs in chroma
  (a recolour, such as another costume's colours, keeps its own
  texture). The game's texture is drawn until then; a match becomes an
  ordinary replacement a frame or two later.
- Matches are kept in textures/.matched/<pack id>.ini in this program's
  keys, in the form of the pack's key (full, any address, or any
  palette), and textures compared with something but matched with
  nothing under [unmatched]; the next session uses them at once.
  Textures no image has the shape of are not decoded.
- find() takes a callback that decodes the texture, called only for a
  quick pack's texture not matched yet. The import accepts quick packs
  and says how they are matched; the menu's status shows the count.
- <PREFIX>_NO_QUICK_MATCH=1 refuses quick packs, as before.
- portablekit_texture_pack_tests checks the scoring, the rule, the
  saved matches and index, and gains --match <pack> <dump> [state] to
  run the matcher over a texture dump.

Tested on Windows with a port's clang and MSVC builds: the texture pack
checks and 21 framework tests (ad hoc ones left out). A community pack
of 2,326 keys and 2,116 images, against 622 dumped textures of menus
and a battle stage: 64 textures matched, each checked by eye and right;
in the game the matches appear in the first session and at once in the
next. A five-key pack without ignoreAddress matched all five. Not
tried: other packs, other games, Linux.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
